🧠 Mental Health Tweet Classification using NLP

🩺 Detecting signs of mental health issues in tweets using Natural Language Processing and Machine Learning
🔍 Overview

This project builds and compares multiple NLP models to classify tweets related to mental health awareness.
Using TF-IDF vectorization and machine learning algorithms such as SVM, Logistic Regression, and Naive Bayes, the goal is to detect whether a tweet reflects mental distress or is neutral.

🧩 Key Features

🧹 Comprehensive Preprocessing using NLTK (lemmatization, stopword removal, cleaning emojis & URLs)

🔠 TF-IDF Vectorization with unigrams and bigrams

⚙️ Multi-model Comparison — Logistic Regression, SVM, Naive Bayes, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting

📊 Confusion Matrices & F1 Comparison Charts

🔎 Error Inspection for misclassified tweets

⚖️ Balanced Training to handle label imbalance
